audit-chain.key

# R76: the ZCode tool's ignore file is a LOCAL tool config, and its content is by
# construction an inventory of what must NOT be published — it names private
# repositories and the private-asset paths they hold. It was tracked, which made
# that inventory shippable with any release tag. Untracked (kept on disk, where
# the tool still reads it); nothing in the tree or the gates depends on it.
# NOTE the trap this sits next to: adding a path here does nothing for an
# ALREADY-TRACKED file, so this entry only holds because `git rm --cached`
# removed it from the index.
.zcodeignore

# NOTE: `evals/` is deliberately NOT ignored. Its JSON overlay names a private
# repository's gold pack, but `tests/dd_adjudication_pins.rs` `include_str!`s it
# and `tests/drift_census_pins.rs` reads `R57_DRIFT_BASELINE.json` at runtime —
# ignoring either would break a fresh clone's build and suite. The private repo
# NAME is scrubbed in place instead (`<private-repo>`), and
# tests/drift_census_pins.rs pins that it stays scrubbed.

# dep-research scratch (crate extraction) — never commit
.depcheck/

# AGENTS.md is deliberately NOT ignored. It is tracked and published (added
# 64abca7; the same blob is in both origin/main and public/main), and public
# source cites it as its authority (src/workflow/channels.rs:19,
# src/workflow/delivery.rs:4151, client/src/main.rs:23) — so it is
# load-bearing, not hidden. An earlier `/AGENTS.md` rule here was INERT:
# .gitignore never applies to an already-tracked file, so it asserted a
# protection the repo did not have. Re-adding the rule would recreate the
# same false control.
docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_20261006_TENTH_PASS.md
docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_20261006_NINTH_PASS.md
docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_20260912_FIFTH_PASS.md
docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_20260912_FOURTH_PASS.md
docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_20260913_SEVENTH_PASS.md
docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_20261006_TENTH_PASS_REGULATORY.md
